  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Stir in pasta and return pot to boil. Cook until al dente. Drain well.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt butter in a large saucepan over medium heat. Stir in garlic and shrimp. Cook, stirring constantly, for 3 to 5 minutes.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in wine and pepper. Bring to a boil and cook for 30 seconds while stirring constantly.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix shrimp with drained pasta in a serving bowl. Sprinkle with cheese and parsley. Serve immediately.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "This is a very tasty but simple recipe. I had some frozen, cooked jumbo shrimp in the freezer, so I just used those and cooked them until heated through. I added 1 cup broccoli and 1/4 cup freshly roasted red peppers to the pasta to make this a one dish meal. I will try adding asparagus next time."
    }
